Nuked OPN2: the envelope and the output without shifting a negative number

Two places shift a negative number left, which is undefined behaviour;
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the program at the first of them as soon as a
note is played:

  src/chips/nuked/ym3438.c:684:31: runtime error: left shift of negative value
  -1024

* The attack step of the envelope scales the complement of the level, which is
  negative for every level below 1024, by the envelope increment. The
  increment is at most 4, so the product is far inside an int.

* The FM output is sign-extended from bit 13 by shifting it left and back
  right. The value that reaches it is within about 16384, so the product is
  well inside a Bit32s and the shift back gives the same number as before.

Multiplications say the same thing and are defined.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/chips/nuked/ym3438.c b/src/chips/nuked/ym3438.c
index b2f75a5..bfc2401 100644
--- a/src/chips/nuked/ym3438.c
+++ b/src/chips/nuked/ym3438.c
@@ -667,7 +667,7 @@ void OPN2_EnvelopeADSR(ym3438_t *chip)
         }
         else if (chip->eg_state[slot] == eg_num_attack && level != 0 && chip->eg_inc && nkon)
         {
-            inc = (~level << chip->eg_inc) >> 5;
+            inc = ((~level) * (1 << chip->eg_inc)) >> 5;
         }
     }
     else
@@ -681,7 +681,7 @@ void OPN2_EnvelopeADSR(ym3438_t *chip)
             }
             else if(chip->eg_inc && !chip->eg_ratemax && nkon)
             {
-                inc = (~level << chip->eg_inc) >> 5;
+                inc = ((~level) * (1 << chip->eg_inc)) >> 5;
             }
             break;
         case eg_num_decay:
@@ -1084,7 +1084,7 @@ void OPN2_FMGenerate(ym3438_t *chip)
     {
         output = output ^ (chip->mode_test_21[4] << 13);
     }
-    output <<= 2;
+    output *= 4;
     output >>= 2;
     chip->fm_out[slot] = output;
 }
